    array.push(cD, "S-9,S-5,S8,P9,S10,X-3,S-5,W-4,X-1,T0,P-6,C-4,T1,X3,P4,T-2,T0,W5,P5,P6,T2,P7,X3,P4,C5,X-2,T-1,X-1,F-3")
    array.push(cH, "Wall Street had its worst day in weeks, and the dollar still walked away with the stronger hand.|Sterling slept through the night while American shares tumbled, and the greenback kept its edge.|Tokyo's inflation came in a touch cooler than hoped, and the yen lost another piece of its story.|The fear gauge closed well above 25, and that is the franc's alarm bell ringing for real this time.|No news from Ottawa overnight, and the loonie's case stayed as soft as it was on Thursday.|The Aussie's bad week found no relief overnight, so the bearish shadow from Thursday holds.|The kiwi had no headlines of its own, which left the dollar to set the tone again.|Neither side spoke overnight, so this pair waits on London's shoppers and Lagarde's microphone.|Japan's softer core inflation took the bite out of the yen, and the bearish lean here slipped into a stand-off.|A genuine risk-off close lands right on this pair's fault line, but the scores have not moved yet.|The Aussie is still limping after Thursday's jobs shock, which keeps this bearish view under strain.|Two quiet currencies met overnight, and the bearish read stayed exactly where it was.|Still a stand-off: the euro's French trouble and the loonie's soft inflation cancel each other out.|A softer Japanese inflation print turned this stand-off into a pound lean, at least in the shadow.|The franc's fear trigger has now been met on a close, and that leans hard against this pound lean.|A stand-off between two leaking boats: the pound's soft inflation and the Aussie's jobs shock.|Level pegging again, with neither side giving the other an opening overnight.|The pound's softer week keeps this bullish view under watch, even with the loonie still weak.|Japan's cooler core CPI helped this pair on paper, but the Aussie's wound keeps it under pressure.|Weak Australian jobs on one side and a risk-off close on the other: this lean is under fire twice.|Still a draw, and the Aussie's weak jobs make a kiwi lean more likely than an Aussie one.|The Aussie's jobs hit keeps pressure on this bullish view, even though the loonie offered no help overnight.|The yen slipped on softer inflation, and this quiet stand-off tipped into a kiwi lean in the shadow.|A true risk-off close puts this kiwi lean on shaky ground ahead of Friday's measurement.|Two quiet commodity currencies, and the kiwi still holds the better hand.|The yen's soft inflation cut away the support under this bearish view, and the shadow now shows a stand-off.|Still a stand-off on the scores, but a risk-off regime tonight could break it toward the franc.|Japan's softer core inflation pulled the yen down, and this bearish lean drifted into a stand-off.|Gold kept sliding through a stock-market rout, so the haven story has not saved it yet.")
